values ((select id from public.teams limit 1), $il$i000$il$, $il$READ FIRST: suggested build order, because several of these block each other$il$, $il$Data & schema$il$, $il$Both$il$, $il$must$il$, $il$open$il$, $il$Claude$il$, '2026-09-01T00:00:00.000Z'::timestamptz, null, '{}'::text[], '{}'::text[], null, null, false, false, $il${"Oliver": "2026-09-09T11:28:43.974Z"}$il$::jsonb,
$il$Several of these block each other. Switch Group by to Build order, or just look at the list as it stands: items now nest under whatever unblocks them, so you can see at a glance that one job frees four others. Tick this off once the order is agreed. It is a plan, not a piece of build.$il$,
$il$Not an improvement, a sequencing note. There are 17 must haves and they are not independent, so working down the list in the order they were raised means building some of them twice. This is a suggested order, argue with it.

WAVE 0 - UNBLOCK
  i001 Supabase MCP connector via Paul. Gates the research agent entirely, and with it i008, i014, i025 and i029. Nothing in wave 3 or the agent side starts without it.

WAVE 1 - SCHEMA AND DATA TRUTH, before anything reads it
  i031 Split LinkedIn URL from Sales Nav URL, backfill, and make record-at-send a hard rule
  i002 product_line enum on companies AND contacts
  i006 Estimates structurally separate from stated figures, is_estimate flag
  i018 Widen the Reply Classification enum
  i010 Fix connection status mirroring
  WHY FIRST: everything downstream reads these. Getting them wrong now means a data migration later rather than an edit. i018 in particular is an enum decision, and it is the reason the success metric is currently unmeasurable, so it is cheap now and expensive after there is data in it.

WAVE 2 - THE GUARDS, all failing closed
  i005 Fail closed as the pattern for every guard, null blocks and never passes
  i004 Group level duplicate approach guard
  i030 A send derives status to Contacted, forward only, plus the reconciliation of the ten wrong rows
  WHY SECOND: outreach is happening now, and these are what stop it going wrong. i005 is the pattern the other two are built on, so it goes first within the wave.

WAVE 3 - THE DERIVED STATE LAYER
  i029 Research stage goes Outdated on age, and the research queue
  i025 Comments and instructions field feeding THE SAME queue, build one not two
  i003 next_step replacing P0/P1/P3
  WHY IN THIS ORDER: i003 derives from the states the other two create. Build next_step before Outdated exists and it has nothing to read. i025 and i029 are one piece of plumbing with two entry points, so do them together or the second one rebuilds the first.

WAVE 4 - DRAFTING QUALITY
  i007 Wire the four layer draft stack
  i026 Subject lines generated with the draft, including the message type matrix
  i008 Hold the four layers as versioned rows in Supabase, needs i001
  WHY HERE: the drafts already work well enough to send. This makes them right rather than makes them possible.

WAVE 5 - USABILITY, low risk and parallelisable, drop into any gap
  i028 Long text truncation, the biggest single readability win
  i032 Jump buttons to LinkedIn and Sales Nav, NEEDS i031 first or it is dead for a third of contacts
  i011 Source leads for these companies as a Today headline
  i009 Move to Monday button, retires a 70 pound a month tool
  i022 Inline editing, i023 column widths, i027 Countries multi select, i016 delete button, i024 link rot

WAVE 6 - NEW CAPABILITY
  i012 Funnel view
  i013 Campaigns, which is also where the revised cooldown lives
  i014 Buying signals, needs i001
  i015 Email and phone enrichment, needs i031 because it looks up on the /in/ URL

DUPLICATE TO CLOSE: i017 'LinkedIn button on the contact card' is now covered by i032, which does both surfaces and both URL types. Tick i017 off against i032 rather than building it twice.

THE THREE PARKED ITEMS are decisions and cautions rather than work: i019 do not automate LinkedIn deep links, i020 title matching alone picks the wrong people at scale, i021 calibrate the 1.5 percent conversion rate against a real partner. i021 is the highest value measurement available to us and only Oliver can trigger it, by asking one partner for their visits to orders ratio.$il$);
