insert into public.improvements (team_id, item_key, title, category, owner, priority, status, raised_by, created_at, build_wave, blocks, blocked_by, done_by, done_at, pinned, hidden, seen_by, detail, notes)
values ((select id from public.teams limit 1), $il$i001$il$, $il$Connectors are added, but Oliver cannot log in$il$, $il$Integrations$il$, $il$Both$il$, $il$blocker$il$, $il$open$il$, $il$Oliver$il$, '2026-09-08T16:00:00.000Z'::timestamptz, 0, array[$il$i008$il$,$il$i014$il$,$il$i025$il$,$il$i029$il$]::text[], '{}'::text[], null, null, false, false, $il${"Brad": "2026-09-20T14:40:41.450Z", "Oliver": "2026-09-15T13:06:51.416Z"}$il$::jsonb,
$il$Moved on, still blocking. Paul has added the Supabase and Lovable connectors to Oliver's Claude, so the admin permission part is closed. Oliver now cannot log in, so the research agent still cannot reach Supabase and nothing downstream of this has been unblocked in practice.

Next step, agreed 9 September: Oliver and Brad walk through it on a screenshare rather than trading messages about it. There is a short list of the usual causes in the background below, worth having open during the call so it takes ten minutes rather than an hour.$il$,
$il$WHAT TO ESTABLISH FIRST, because these are four different failures wearing the same face:
1. Which login is actually failing. The connector's OAuth handshake to Supabase, the Lovable connector, or signing in to the Supabase dashboard directly in a browser. Try the plain dashboard login first, outside Claude. If that fails too, this is not a Claude problem at all and the call should be with Paul, not Brad.
2. Whether Oliver has a Supabase account WITH ACCESS TO THE PROJECT. Adding a connector to the workspace and being a member of the Supabase organisation are separate things. Paul may have done the first and not the second, which would look exactly like this.
3. Same question for Lovable: does Oliver hold a seat on the actual project, or only an account.
4. Which Claude surface is being used. A connector added org wide can still need enabling for the individual user, and claude.ai and Claude Code do not always present the same list.

TWO THINGS THAT CATCH PEOPLE OUT, worth checking before anything more elaborate:
A second signed in identity in the browser will silently capture an OAuth redirect, so the handshake completes against the wrong account and then denies access. Try it in a private window. Oliver has had a dotless alias account cause exactly this kind of confusion before.
If Pier uses Microsoft single sign on, Supabase has to be entered through the right identity provider. Signing in with email and password on an account that was created through SSO fails in a way that reads as a bad password.

WHAT TO CAPTURE ON THE CALL, so this item can be closed honestly: the exact error text, which of the four logins above it came from, and who owns the fix. If it turns out to be a Supabase org invite, that is Paul again and the item stays open until he has done it.

STILL THE SAME DEPENDENCY. This continues to gate i008, i014, i025 and i029. Nothing changes there until Oliver is actually signed in, so do not treat the connectors being present as this item being done.

HISTORY, the original block, now cleared: Oliver is a member, not an admin, of the Pier Claude team workspace, and only admins can add custom connectors. Paul owns the workspace and needed to add it org wide. Brad asked Paul, and Paul has done it.$il$);
