insert into public.improvements (team_id, item_key, title, category, owner, priority, status, raised_by, created_at, build_wave, blocks, blocked_by, done_by, done_at, pinned, hidden, seen_by, detail, notes)
values ((select id from public.teams limit 1), $il$i002$il$, $il$Ticketplan and Pier Protect must be separable$il$, $il$Data & schema$il$, $il$Brad$il$, $il$must$il$, $il$open$il$, $il$Oliver$il$, '2026-09-08T16:01:00.000Z'::timestamptz, 1, array[$il$i039$il$]::text[], '{}'::text[], null, null, false, false, $il${"Oliver": "2026-09-09T11:29:08.359Z"}$il$::jsonb,
$il$Ticket.io landed in the Pier Protect lake and is a Ticketplan company. On 17 September Oliver hit it again: Veronika Pfeiffer is a Ticketplan contact sitting in the Pending Review queue in Pier Lead Lake, with a draft written for her, and nothing on the row says which product she belongs to. He only knows because he remembers.

WHAT IS NEEDED

1. A PRODUCT FIELD ON THE COMPANY, as an enum: Pier Protect, Ticketplan, Both, Other, Unknown. This is the company's home book. Contacts and touches inherit it, and a contact can override it, because one person at one company can be worked for the other product.

2. THE COMPANY HEADER SHOWS IT, next to the name, not buried in a field list. Oliver asked for this in those words: it has to be clear where a company mainly sits.

3. A BADGE ON EVERY OUTREACH ROW AND CONTACT CARD. Small, always visible, never hidden behind a filter. The badge is what prevents a mistake; a filter only helps when you remember to set it.

4. A PRODUCT SWITCH AT THE TOP OF THE APP: Pier Protect, Ticketplan, Both. It filters every view, not only Outreach, and it stays set while Oliver moves between Companies, Contacts, Outreach and Today, because the point is to focus on one book for a stretch of work. Default Both, with the badges on, so nothing is ever silently hidden.

5. EVERY COUNT RESPECTS IT. Volume, Pending Review, Awaiting Reply, reply rate, momentum. Those five numbers on the Outreach header are currently two products added together, which makes each of them true of nothing.

BACKFILL IS LIST-BASED, NOT A GUESS PER RECORD. The Ticketplan contacts came in from the Ticketplan book and the Ticketplan monday workspace, so they can be marked as a set. Anything not on that list is Pier Protect until someone says otherwise. Unknown is a value Brad can filter on, not a blank.$il$,
$il$PRODUCT IS NOT A LABEL, IT IS A ROUTING KEY. This is the argument for a schema field rather than a coloured chip. Almost everything downstream already differs by product and the system currently cannot tell:

  THE PITCH DIFFERS. Pier Protect sells device protection into retailers and telcos. Ticketplan sells refund protection into ticketing and events. A draft written from the Pier Protect wedge and sent to a ticketing contact is not slightly off, it is about the wrong product.

  THE VOICE DIFFERS. Ticketplan has its own identity and must not carry Pier branding. Ticketplan German writes du by default; Pier Protect does not.

  THE CHANNEL RULES DIFFER. Ticketplan email goes through monday, because there is no Outlook access on the Ticketplan address. So an email route proposed for a Ticketplan contact is one Oliver cannot actually use.

  THE SCORING DIFFERS. Annual devices sold, refurbished, SIM-free, and the deal heuristic at 8 percent on phones and 6 percent on laptops and tablets mean nothing for a ticketing platform. The company scoring in i071 will rank Ticketplan companies on Pier Protect inputs and produce nonsense unless it knows which book it is scoring.

SO THE FIELD DOES FOUR JOBS: it picks the wedge, the voice, the channel and the scoring model.

IT ALSO MATTERS FOR REPORTING. Pier Protect and Ticketplan are separate lines for Oliver, so any read of how the pipeline is doing has to be per product. At the moment no number in the system can be split.

AND THE CONNECTION REQUEST BUDGET IS SHARED WHILE THE PRODUCTS ARE NOT. Twenty a day, see i072, spent across two books with no way to say how many went to each. That is what i039 is about, and it cannot be built until this field exists.

SAME PATTERN AS i041, i086 AND i093. Product and pipeline position are independent facts, so they are two fields. Worth saying because the tempting shortcut is to encode product inside an existing status, a list name or a tag, and it will break the same way.

ONE THING TO WATCH. Both is a real value, not a fudge. A large events retailer could genuinely be worked for both. It should be rare and deliberate, and if the backfill produces a lot of Both, that means the list was not clean, not that the companies are ambiguous.$il$);

